	(lib_symbols)
	(text "# BLOCK DIAGRAM & SUBSYSTEM INTERCONNECT DESIGN NOTES\nProject: BLEBridge Board\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe top-level block diagram outlines the system interconnect topology and power distribution across five functional sheets: USB-C, BATTERY, MCU, \nREGULATOR, and LoRa. All power domains and signal paths reference a unified system ground (GND) to simplify return paths \nand maximize board-level signal integrity.\n\n---\n\n1. TOP-LEVEL INTERCONNECT ARCHITECTURE\n- USB-C Interface: USB_C sheet exports the USB_DATA(USB_D+ USB_D-) bus to the MCU sheet. This is the native USB 2.0 full-speed differential \n  pair after USBLC6-25C6 ESD array clamping and 27 ohm series impedance-matching resistors.\n- Battery & Fuel Gauge Interface: BATTERY sheet exports the I2C_BUS(SDA SCL) shared telemetry lines and active-LOW BATT_ALERT interrupt signal \n  to the MCU sheet.\n- LoRa Radio Control & Data Bus: MCU sheet exports SPI(SPI_MOSI, SPI_SCK, SPI_MISO, SPI_NSS), BUSY_LoRa, RESET_LoRa, and DIO10 control lines \n  to the LoRa sheet.\n- System Power Distribution: REGULATOR sheet acts as the global power distribution block, stepping down primary VDD into +3.3V (digital) \n  and +3.3VA (analog) rails.\n- Unified Ground Topology: All functional schematic blocks reference a single common system GND return plane, eliminating separate GNDA \n  or star-ground tie resistors.\n\n---\n\n2. POWER ARCHITECTURE & RAIL ROUTING\n- Primary Power Input: USB-C VBUS feeds directly into the BQ24075 standalone charger and power-path manager on the BATTERY sheet.\n- System Supply Rail (VDD): Main power-path output rail VDD feeds both buck-boost switching regulators on the REGULATOR sheet.\n- Battery Connection (+BATT): Single-cell LiPo/Li-ion battery rail +BATT connects to BQ24075 BAT terminal for dynamic charging \n  and MAX17048 fuel gauge CELL input for state-of-charge telemetry.\n- Dual Buck-Boost Regulators: U2 (TPS63020DSJR) converts VDD into +3.3V for MCU and digital logic; U3 (TPS63020DSJR) converts \n  VDD into +3.3VA for sensitive analog/RF circuitry.\n- Ground Verification: Both +3.3V and +3.3VA rails reference the common ground plane across all board layers.\n\n---\n\n3. COMPLETE INTERFACE MATRIX\n| Net / Bus Signal | Source Block | Destination Block | Signal Function & Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| USB_DATA(USB_D+ USB_D-) | USB-C (J1) | MCU (U6) | Native USB 2.0 data pair, ESD-protected and series-matched. |\n| I2C_BUS(SDA SCL) | BATTERY (U5) | MCU (U6) | Shared I2C bus for MAX17048 fuel gauge state-of-charge telemetry. |\n| BATT_ALERT | BATTERY (U5) | MCU (U6) | Active-LOW fuel gauge state-of-charge interrupt line. |\n| SPI(SPI_MOSI, SPI_SCK, SPI_MISO, SPI_NSS) | MCU (U6) | LoRa (U9) | High-speed SPI data and chip-select bus for SX1262 transceiver. |\n| BUSY_LoRa | LoRa (U16) | MCU (U6) | Transceiver busy handshake status line. |\n| RESET_LoRa | MCU (U6) | LoRa (U9) | Active-LOW transceiver hardware reset control line. |\n| DIO10 | LoRa (U16) | MCU (U6) | Transceiver interrupt request line (DIO1). |\n| VDD | BATTERY (U4) | REGULATOR (U2/U3) | System power output rail from BQ24075 power-path manager. |\n| +3.3V | REGULATOR (U2) | MCU / Digital Peripherals | Main regulated digital power supply rail. |\n| +3.3VA | REGULATOR (U3) | LoRa / Analog Peripherals | Dedicated low-noise analog power supply rail referenced to common GND. |\n| GND | All Sheets | All Sheets | Common system ground return for USB-C, BATTERY, MCU, LoRa, and REGULATOR. |"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
